about='''<section class="page-hero"><div class="container"><span class="eyebrow">Why Agent Lab exists</span><h1 class="page-title">Less AI noise.<br>More working knowledge.</h1><p>Every day brings new tools, demos, and dramatic promises. Agent Lab focuses instead on the question: what can a person actually build or improve with AI today?</p></div></section><section class="section" style="padding-top:20px"><div class="container"><div class="content-grid"><div class="content-panel"><h2>What we're building</h2><p>A searchable library of practical AI playbooks, with context, implementation steps, documentation references, and caution notes.</p><p>We want to make useful AI more understandable to creators, teams, and small businesses. Agent Lab starts as a curated publication; community discussion, content submissions, and richer tools can follow when we can support them reliably.</p><a class="button primary" href="/directory/">Explore the directory ↗</a></div><div class="content-panel"><h2>What we won't do</h2><ul><li>Promise that using AI will make you a particular amount of money.</li><li>Publish fake case studies or invented community activity.</li><li>Claim a sponsored listing is an independent endorsement.</li><li>Present an editorial estimate as a measured result.</li></ul></div></div><div class="section-spacer"></div><div id="standards" class="content-panel"><span class="eyebrow">How we publish</span><h2>Editorial standards</h2><p><strong>Primary documentation first.</strong> Each initial directory entry links to at least one relevant vendor-maintained resource. These sources support the tools' capabilities, not a guarantee that every proposed workflow will work for every reader.</p><p><strong>Specific and testable.</strong> A useful guide describes the user problem, basic setup, tradeoffs, and an initial verification step. Setup times are editorial estimates and may vary.</p><p><strong>Transparent commercial relationships.</strong> Paid placements and affiliate relationships will be identified near their links or content. Sponsors cannot purchase favorable editorial conclusions.</p><p><strong>Corrections and safety.</strong> Readers should verify facts, protect private information, follow applicable terms, and retain human review for important decisions. Requests for corrections can be sent through our <a class="plain-link" href="/sponsor/#inquiry">contact form</a> once email delivery is configured.</p><p class="disclaimer">Agent Lab is a new project. The editorial library exists; audience metrics, a public forum, and automated content operations are not yet established.</p></div></div></section>'''
